# Frontend line-ending authority.
#
# .editorconfig already declares this repository's canonical policy:
#   [*] charset = utf-8-bom, end_of_line = lf
# Editors honour it; git did not. There was no .gitattributes, so core.autocrlf=true
# alone decided checkout and wrote CRLF for these files on Windows — which is why the
# working tree drifted away from the declared policy.
#
# These rules make the existing policy binding for the BOM-managed frontend set only,
# i.e. exactly the set tests/test_frontend_structure.js checks via frontFiles():
# InternalBeyond.html plus every .css / .js under assets/css, assets/js and game.
# Deliberately NO `* text=auto` and no other paths: renormalizing the whole repository
# is not wanted, and every HEAD blob in this scope is already LF, so no stored content
# changes — only how git checks these paths out.
#
# Scope note: this file governs line endings only. The UTF-8 BOM requirement is owned by
# scripts/ib-bom.py and the encoding.bom.* assertions, not by this file.
#
# This file covers itself: core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check .gitattributes out as
# CRLF, and a trailing CR is not something an attribute parser should ever have to tolerate.
# .editorconfig already requires end_of_line = lf for [*], so this only makes it binding.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
InternalBeyond.html text eol=lf
assets/css/**/*.css text eol=lf
assets/js/**/*.js text eol=lf
game/**/*.css text eol=lf
game/**/*.js text eol=lf
